{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\(\\angle XYZ\\) where \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of three edges of a cube, we will use coordinate geometry. Let's start by assigning coordinates to the vertices of the cube.\n\nAssume the cube has side length 2 for simplicity, and place it in a 3D coordinate system with one vertex at the origin \\((0,0,0)\\). The coordinates of the vertices can be:\n\n- \\(A = (0, 0, 0)\\)\n- \\(B = (2, 0, 0)\\)\n- \\(C = (2, 2, 0)\\)\n- \\(D = (0, 2, 0)\\)\n- \\(E = (0, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(F = (2, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(G = (2, 2, 2)\\)\n- \\(H = (0, 2, 2)\\)\n\nThe midpoints of the edges are:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(EG\\) and \\(FH\\), so \\(X = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2}, \\frac{2+2}{2}\\right) = (1, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(EF\\) and \\(DG\\), so \\(Y = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{2+0}{2}\\right) = (1, 1, 1)\\)\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(EH\\) and \\(FG\\), so \\(Z = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{2+0}{2}, \\frac{2+2}{2}\\right) = (1, 1, 2)\\)\n\n","prefix_end":947,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,1124,11520,4044,71089,57758,1380,17767,55,59,701,17767,56,59,701,323,17767,57,57758,525,279,5099,7706,315,2326,12822,315,264,23739,11,582,686,990,16184,17047,13,6771,594,1191,553,60753,13934,311,279,17228,315,279,23739,382,5615,3885,279,23739,702,3108,3084,220,17,369,38975,11,323,1992,432,304,264,220,18,35,16184,1849,448,825,11936,518,279,6238,1124,1188,15,11,15,11,15,10699,568,576,13934,315,279,17228,646,387,1447,12,17767,32,284,320,15,11,220,15,11,220,15,10699,340,12,17767,33,284,320,17,11,220,15,11,220,15,10699,340,12,17767,34,284,320,17,11,220,17,11,220,15,10699,340,12,17767,35,284,320,15,11,220,17,11,220,15,10699,340,12,17767,36,284,320,15,11,220,15,11,220,17,10699,340,12,17767,37,284,320,17,11,220,15,11,220,17,10699,340,12,17767