e-07,-1.1079323291778564,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,-4.172316494077677e-06,0.0,-0.09330645203590393,-9.775113539944869e-06,0.0,-2.0265558760002023e-06,-3.576278118089249e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-4.768370445162873e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.06058523803949356,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-0.13448873162269592,-0.31834810972213745,-0.0007769426447339356,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-5.960446742392378e-06,-0.000105375460407231,-4.887569048150908e-06,-7.068861305015162e-05,-0.17075474560260773,-6.341733387671411e-05,0.0,0.0,-0.029020914807915688,0.0,-0.027880102396011353,-0.8779500722885132,-5.125986263010418e-06,-4.291525328881107e-06,-7.152555099310121e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,81963,315,2326,12822,315,264,23739,525,8433,11,438,6839,3685,13,220,7379,57960,4044,71089,4779,304,12348,271,58,6405,921,25643,551,7,16,13,17,9961,626,12670,362,11,425,11,356,11,422,11,350,11,1599,11,809,11,1863,280,12670,856,11,379,11,1147,401,87,284,320,17,4999,15,13,17,317,88,284,320,16,13,17,11,15,13,23,317,89,284,320,15,11,17,626,55,284,320,15,11,15,317,56,284,856,280,51,284,379,280,32,284,1147,280,57,284,856,488,379,280,33,284,856,488,1147,280,35,284,379,488,1147,280,34,284,856,488,379,488,1147,401,7633,1188,34,488,422,5620,17,313,7,33,488,356,5620,17,313,7,33,488,809,5620,17,11,1151,317,7633,7644,313,56,313,57,313,34,313,35,313,32,313,21621,317,7633,5349,313,32,317,7633,5349,313,34,317,7633,5349,313,56,317,7633,4140,313,55,11991,13571,317,7633,4140,313,35,11991,13571,317,7633,4140,313,57,11991,13571,626,1502,20912,55,73315,320,34,488,422,5620,17,11,451,317,1502,20912,56,73315,320,33,488,356,5620,17,11,5052,317,1502,20912,57,73315,320,33,488,809,5620,17,11,467,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe midpoint of three edges of a cube are connected, as shown below.  Find $\\angle XYZ,$ in degrees\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(1.2 cm);\n\npair A, B, C, D, T, X, Y, Z;\npair x, y, z;\n\nx = (2,-0.2);\ny = (1.2,0.8);\nz = (0,2);\n\nX = (0,0);\nY = x;\nT = y;\nA = z;\nZ = x + y;\nB = x + z;\nD = y + z;\nC = x + y + z;\n\ndraw((C + D)/2--(B + C)/2--(B + Y)/2,red);\ndraw(X--Y--Z--C--D--A--cycle);\ndraw(B--A);\ndraw(B--C);\ndraw(B--Y);\ndraw(T--X,dashed);\ndraw(T--D,dashed);\ndraw(T--Z,dashed);\n\nlabel(\"$X$\", (C + D)/2, N);\nlabel(\"$Y$\", (B + C)/2, SE);\nlabel(\"$Z$\", (B + Y)/2, W);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"c069ae159563ca90e2563d7163ba13556de8e1580801868ba8e2e03f1b263a42"},"seconds":21.84346079826355,"seed":126412348592409207,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\(\\angle XYZ\\) where \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of three edges of a cube, we will use coordinate geometry. Let's start by assigning coordinates to the vertices of the cube.\n\nAssume the cube has side length 2 for simplicity, and place it in a 3D coordinate system with one vertex at the origin \\((0,0,0)\\). The coordinates of the vertices can be:\n\n- \\(A = (0, 0, 0)\\)\n- \\(B = (2, 0, 0)\\)\n- \\(C = (2, 2, 0)\\)\n- \\(D = (0, 2, 0)\\)\n- \\(E = (0, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(F = (2, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(G = (2, 2, 2)\\)\n- \\(H = (0, 2, 2)\\)\n\nThe midpoints of the edges are:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(EG\\) and \\(FH\\), so \\(X = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2}, \\frac{2+2}{2}\\right) = (1, 0, 2)\\)\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(EF\\) and \\(DG\\), so \\(Y = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{2+0}{2}\\right) = (1, 1, 1)\\)\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(EH\\) and \\(FG\\), so \\(Z = \\left(\\frac{0+2}{2}, \\frac{2+0}{2}, \\frac{2+2}{2}\\right) = (1, 1, 2)\\)\n\nNow, we need to find the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{XY}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{XZ}\\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{XY} = Y - X = (1, 1, 1) - (1, 0, 2) = (0, 1, -1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{XZ} = Z - X = (1, 1, 2) - (1, 0, 2) = (0, 1, 0)\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\overrightarrow{XY} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{XZ}\\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{XY} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{XZ} = (0, 1, -1) \\cdot (0, 1, 0) = 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 1 + (-1) \\cdot 0 = 1\n\\]\n\nWe also find the magnitudes of \\(\\overrightarrow{XY}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{XZ}\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{XY}\\| = \\sqrt{0^2 + 1^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{XZ}\\| = \\sqrt{0^2 + 1^2 + 0^2} = 1\n\\]\n\nUsing the dot product formula \\(\\overrightarrow{a} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{b} = \\|\\overrightarrow{a}\\| \\|\\overrightarrow{b}\\| \\cos \\theta\\), we solve for \\(\\cos \\theta\\):\n\\[\n1 = \\sqrt{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\cos \\theta \\implies \\cos \\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe angle \\(\\theta\\) whose cosine is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\theta = 45^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the angle \\(\\angle XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{45}\\) degrees."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{45}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:7"}
